-- demand-wall.rofl with an aggregate, so the reference explains it with
-- src/aggeval.ts rather than src/api.ts: the same wall, through the other
-- explainer (scripts/whycheck.ts). That evaluator does ask `up(1)` and
-- leaves a depth shrug, which the reference's load writes under `$load(N)`
-- and rofl load under `$adhoc` (one evaluation at the end: the `budget_wall`
-- contract difference) — so this world is asked no excise, whose diff would
-- carry that attribution and nothing about explanation.
edb(k).
up(X) :- Y is X + 1, up(Y).
q(a).
q(b).
r(X) :- q(X), not k(X), up(1), k(X).
s(X) :- q(X).
nq(N) :- N is count(X : s(X)).
